<!-- newsletter-confirmation — the double opt-in step (039 US6).

     ⚠ THIS MESSAGE IS THE CONSENT, not a notification that consent was recorded. Nobody is subscribed
     until the link in it is followed. That is what makes the subscribe form safe to leave open to
     anonymous visitors: a stranger can type someone else's address into it and the only consequence is
     that the address's real owner receives one ignorable email. Without this step the same form is a
     tool for subscribing other people.

     ⚠ TRANSACTIONAL, DELIBERATELY, AND THIS IS THE ONE THAT INVITES ARGUMENT. It carries no
     unsubscribe footer, and that looks wrong for anything newsletter-shaped. But an unsubscribe link
     here would be an unsubscribe from a subscription that DOES NOT YET EXIST — there is nothing to
     leave. The recipient's way out is simply to ignore it, which is stronger than any link. The moment
     the platform sends an actual campaign, that message is `lifecycle` and the catalogue's type system
     will REFUSE to let it compile without an unsubscribe URL.

     ⚠ NO DISCOUNT. The reference storefront's newsletter band promises "Get 20% Off On Your First
     Purchase". Effy has no such promotion, and FR-034 forbids inventing one — a discount claim in an
     opt-in email is a contract with the reader. -->

<mjml lang="en" dir="ltr">
  <mj-head>
    <mj-include path="../generated/theme.mjml" />
    <mj-title>Confirm your {{effyProductName}} updates</mj-title>
    <mj-preview>One tap to confirm, and we&rsquo;ll keep you posted.</mj-preview>
  </mj-head>

  <mj-body width="600px" background-color="#f5f5f5" css-class="e-bg-page">
    <mj-include path="../components/header.mjml" />

    <mj-section padding="0 32px 32px 32px">
      <mj-column>
        <mj-text mj-class="h1" css-class="e-ink e-h1">
          Confirm your subscription
        </mj-text>

        <mj-text mj-class="muted" css-class="e-muted" padding="12px 0 0 0">
          Someone entered this address to hear about new products and offers from {{effyProductName}}.
          Confirm below and we&rsquo;ll start sending.
        </mj-text>

        <!-- Both dark classes named so the label inverts with the fill — 038 shipped a receipt button
             that was invisible in dark mode because the class landed on the wrapping <td> while the
             colour sat on an inner element. -->
        <mj-button href="{{confirmUrl}}" css-class="e-btn-bg e-btn-fg" align="left" padding="24px 0 0 0">
          Confirm subscription
        </mj-button>

        <mj-text mj-class="small" css-class="e-muted" padding="20px 0 0 0">
          This link expires in {{expiresIn}}. If it has, just subscribe again from our site.
        </mj-text>

        <!-- ⚠ The line that makes an unrequested email harmless, and it must never become an
             apology or an instruction. There is nothing for them to do. -->
        <mj-text mj-class="small" css-class="e-muted" padding="12px 0 0 0">
          Didn&rsquo;t sign up? Ignore this email &mdash; nothing was added and we won&rsquo;t write again.
        </mj-text>
      </mj-column>
    </mj-section>

    <mj-include path="../components/footer.mjml" />
  </mj-body>
</mjml>
